# QUESTION : CACHING KI ZARURAT KYA HAI ? - REPEATED DATABASE READS
======================================================================

Product Service ke paas API hai:

    GET /products/{product_id}

Ab maan lo Product jiski product_id = 101 hai wo popular hai, aur 1000 users 
same product request karte hain.

1000 Requests  →  1000 Database Reads

Same data baar-baar DB se read ho raha hai, even though Product 101 ki info 
frequently change nahi hoti.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
## QUESTION: REPEATED READS KE LIYE BAAR-BAAR DB HIT KARNA KYUN PROBLEM HAI ?
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Frequently accessed data ke liye har baar Database ko hit karna unnecessarily expensive ho sakta hai 
kyunki har DB request process karne me multiple resources consume hote hain:


1. NETWORK COMMUNICATION
-------------------------

- Agar Application aur Database different servers par deployed hain, to Application DB query ko network ke
  through DB tak bhejta hai, phir query execute hoti hai aur uska result network ke through wapas Application 
  tak aata hai. Is wajah se har request pe network latency ka overhead introduce hota hai.

- Agar Application aur Database same server par deployed hain,
  to communication machine ke andar hi hota hai across different
  ports of the server.Physical network par data bahar nahi jaata,
  lekin communication cost completely zero nahi hoti.


2. CPU USAGE
------------

Database query process karne ke liye CPU computation karta hai. Jaise:

- Data locate karna — required row kis DB page me hai, wo page RAM (Buffer Pool) me hai ya nahi — ye determine karna
- Index check karna — query jis column pe row dhoondh rahi hai, us pe index hai ya nahi — agar hai to wo index page RAM me hai ya nahi
- Filter, Sorting, Aggregation, Joins — WHERE, ORDER BY, SUM(amount) , JOIN — multiple rows par calculations

Same frequently requested data ke liye database query baar-baar execute hone par database CPU resources 
repeatedly consume / waste hote hain.



3. DATA ACCESS COST — DISK vs RAM (Buffer Pool)
---------------------------------------------------

Database ka persistent data disk (SSD/HDD) pe stored hota hai.
Lekin Database directly har query ke liye disk se read nahi karta,
Database frequently accessed data ko RAM ke Buffer Pool me store karta hai, 
taaki har baar disk se data read na karna pade.
kyunki disk access RAM se significantly slower hota hai.

Database Buffer Pool = RAM ka woh area jahan Database
data/index pages ko temporarily store karta hai.


### QUESTION: DB / INDEX PAGES KYA HOTE HAI ?
----------------------------------------------

- Database data ko fixed-size units, called pages, me store karta hai. Matlab kisi bhi actual table
  data ko DBMS multiple DB pages ke form me disk par store karta hai.
- Index pages me database indexes ka data stored hota hai, jiska use Database required rows ko
  efficiently locate karne ke liye karta hai.
- Query process karte waqt required data pages aur index pages ko disk se RAM (Buffer Pool) me load kiya jaata hai, 
  uske baad us par query ke hisaab se operation perform kiye jaate hain.

### NOTE : 
------------
Data/Index Pages, Buffer Pool, aur data access mechanism detail me DB module 
me cover kiya hai yahan sirf cost pe focus kar rahe hain.



### QUESTION: COST KYA HAI ?
-----------------------------

Agar simultaneously bahut saari READ queries execute ho rahi hain, to database ki available RAM
par memory pressure increase ho sakta hai. Kyunki un read requests ke corresponding data pages aur 
index pages ko disk se RAM (Buffer Pool) me load karna padta hai kisi bhi operation se pehle. 
Matlab jitni zyada read requests, utne zyada I/O operations disk se pages fetch karne ke liye.
Is wajah se additional I/O latency overhead create hota hai, kyunki disk RAM se slow hoti hai.
Aur kyunki Database ki RAM limited hoti hai, agar RAM full ho jaati hai, to naye data/index pages ko RAM me
laane ke liye hume purane pages (data/index) ko RAM (Buffer Pool) se evict karna padta hai. Aur agar
baad me un evicted pages ki zarurat pade, to dobara disk se load karna padta hai — ye extra I/O latency overhead hai.


### IMPORTANT:
----------------
- Caching ka primary benefit read-heavy workloads me hota hai — especially jab same data frequently read kiya ja raha ho.
  Repeated Reads → Cache → Database Reads Reduce
- Write operations pe caching ka koi impact nahi hota — business data ultimately Database me update karna hi padta hai.
  Write Request → Application → Database





