# QUESTION: REDIS SCALING KI ZAROORAT KAB PADTI HAI?
======================================================

- Small to medium scale systems me ek single Redis instance sufficient hota hai. Wo saari cache keys store karta hai, 
  aur read/write dono requests handle karta hai.

- Lekin jaise-jaise traffic badhta hai aur cached data ki quantity increase hoti hai, ye single Redis instance dheere-dheere 
  bottleneck ban jaata hai. Uske paas limited memory hoti hai, limited throughput hoti hai, aur sabse badi problem wo ek single 
  point of failure ban jaata hai. Agar wo crash ho gaya, to poora cache layer down ho jaayega, aur application directly Database 
  pe load daalega. Isliye jab traffic aur cached data badhta hai, to ek single Redis instance kaafi nahi hota. Tab hume Redis 
  scaling karni padti hai.


-----------------------------------------------
## QUESTION: REDIS KO SCALE KAISE KARTE HAIN ?
-----------------------------------------------

Redis ko scale karne ke 2 tarike hain :

1. VERTICAL SCALING
--------------------

- Vertical Scaling me hum existing Redis server ko zyada powerful bana dete hain — jaise 8 GB RAM aur 4 cores wale node 
  ko upgrade karke 64 GB RAM aur 16 cores wala bana dena — same Redis node, bas uski capacity badh jaati hai.

- BENEFITS :
   1: Simple to implement
   2: Application architecture me koi change nahi karna padta 

- LIMITATIONS :
   1: Ek server ki hardware limit hoti hai uske beyond nahi ja sakte. 
   2: Hardware upgrade ke time server ko temporarily off karna padta hai, aur upgrade ke baad restart karna padta hai — isme downtime create hota hai
   3: Kyunki ye ek hi node hai, ye single point of failure bhi rehta hai — agar ye crash ho gaya to poora caching layer down

- Isliye vertical scaling tab use karo jab traffic abhi kam hai aur architecture simple rakhna hai. 


2. HORIZONTAL SCALING 
-----------------------

- Existing Redis server ko powerful banane ke bajaye, multiple Redis nodes use karo aur data ko un nodes ke across store karo. 
  Ye saare nodes primary hote hain aur high availability ke liye hote hain. Generally Redis Cluster ke andar har primary node 
  ka apna ek replica bhi hota hai.

- Default configuration: Primary Node read aur write dono handle karta hai apne set of data ke liye, aur Replica sirf HA ke liye hota hai
  yaani agar Primary Node fail ho jaye, to Replica promote ho jaata hai.

- Doosri configuration (Read Replicas): Hum ye bhi configure kar sakte hain ki Primary Node sirf writes handle kare apne data ke liye, aur uske Replicas
