## QUESTION: REDIS CLUSTER ME DATA DISTRIBUTION KAISE HOTI HAI?
-----------------------------------------------------------------

Redis Cluster me ye decision Hash Slots ke through hota hai. Simple 3-step process hai.

Step 1: Har key ko hash function me daalte hain, jo ek unique number return karta hai.

     key = user:101
     hash("user:101") = 5432


Step 2: Ab har hash ko slot me convert karte hain. Redis Cluster me 16384 slots hote hain (fixed number).

     slot = hash(key) % 16384

     user:101 → 5432  % 16384 = 5432
     user:102 → 12000 % 16384 = 12000
     user:103 → 8000  % 16384 = 8000

    Ab har key ka ek slot number hai (0 se 16383 ke beech).


Step 3: Ab slot se correct node identify karna hota hai. Redis Cluster khud ye mapping maintain karta hai — kaunsa slot kis node pe hai.

    Node 1 → Slots : 0     - 5460
    Node 2 → Slots : 5461  - 10922
    Node 3 → Slots : 10923 - 16383

    Ab dekho key kahan jayegi:

    user:101 → slot 5432  → Node 1 ✅
    user:102 → slot 12000 → Node 3 ✅
    user:103 → slot 8000  → Node 2 ✅

    IMPORTANT — Same key hamesha same node pe: Kyunki hash(key) hamesha same value dega → same slot → same node.
   


## QUESTION: REDIS CLUSTER ME NODE ADD/REMOVE PE KYA HOTA HAI?
---------------------------------------------------------------

Jab Redis Cluster me naya node add hota hai ya koi node remove hota hai, to slots dobara distribute hote hain
kyunki total 16384 slots ko ab naye node count ke hisaab se baantna hota hai.

Example — 3 se 4 nodes:

 Before (3 nodes):
  Node 1 → Slots : 0     - 5460
  Node 2 → Slots : 5461  - 10922
  Node 3 → Slots : 10923 - 16383

 After (4 nodes):
  Node 1 → Slots : 0     - 4095
  Node 2 → Slots : 4096  - 8191
  Node 3 → Slots : 8192  - 12287
  Node 4 → Slots : 12288 - 16383


Is case me sirf affected slots ka data migrate karna padta hai — as per new mapping. Jaise pehle Node 1 me user_id 0 se 5460 tak ka user data cached tha, 
lekin ab naye mapping ke hisaab se Node 1 pe sirf 0 se 4095 tak ka hi data rahega. Matlab slots 4096 se 5460 wale user_id ka data ab Node 2 me jaana chahiye
kyunki naye mapping me ye slots Node 2 ke range me aate hain. Isliye un affected slots ka data Node 1 se Node 2 me migrate karna padta hai.
Baaki slots (0-4095) ka data Node 1 pe hi rehta hai — unhe migrate nahi karna padta.


### IMPORTANT:
---------------
Migration ke dauran cluster available rehta hai — reads/writes continue chalte rehte hain. 
Redis Cluster slot-by-slot migrate karta hai, isliye downtime nahi hota.



## QUESTION: REDIS CLUSTER ME KEY KO STORE KAISE KARTE HAIN?
-------------------------------------------------------------

Jab Application ko koi data store karna hota hai tab wo pehle apne predefined naming convention ke basis par Cache Key construct karti hai (jaise product:101, user:101).
Phir Redis Client (jo Application ke andar run hota hai — jaise Lettuce ya Jedis) us key ka hash calculate karta hai, hash ko slot me convert karta hai, aur apni cached
slot-to-node mapping se correct Redis Node identify karta hai. Client us node pe SET command bhejta hai aur key use Node pe store ho jaati hai.


## QUESTION: REDIS CLUSTER ME KEY KO RETRIEVE KAISE KARTE HAIN?
-----------------------------------------------------------------

- Jab Application ko koi data chahiye hota hai, wo pehle apne predefined naming convention ke basis par Cache Key construct karti hai (jaise product:101, user:101). 
  Phir Redis Client us key ka hash calculate karta hai, hash ko slot me convert karta hai, aur apni cached slot-to-node mapping se correct Redis Node identify karta hai.
  Client us node pe GET command bhejta hai.

- Agar key mil jaati hai (Cache Hit), to data directly Application ko return kar diya jaata hai.

- Agar key nahi milti (Cache Miss), to Application Database se data fetch karti hai, wahi naming convention use karke same Cache Key construct karti hai, 
  aur Redis Client same slot-to-node mapping ke basis par correct Redis Node identify karke SET command se data store karta hai. Uske baad Application 
  response return kar deti hai.

- Slot-to-node mapping ka actual source of truth Redis Cluster hota hai. Redis Client (jaise Lettuce ya Jedis) sirf uski cached copy rakhta hai (topology fetch karke),
  taaki har request pe cluster se na poochna pade. Agar topology stale ho jaye (node add/remove), to Redis Client galat node pe request bhejta hai
  Redis node usse MOVED / ASK response deta hai.

   -> MOVED = "Slot permanently shift ho gaya — apni topology update karo."
   -> ASK = "Slot abhi migrate ho raha hai — sirf is key ke liye naye node pe try karo, topology mat badlo."



